      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The stunning 2km Bondi to Tamarama coastal walk has again been transformed into a giant sculpture park. This year’s Sculpture by the Sea marks 30 years since the first exhibition in 1997. It’s grown to become known as the world’s largest free outdoor sculpture exhibition and a traditional way to experience the start of summer in Sydney. Here’s a look back at some favourite pieces",
